# Architecture Deep Dive<font></font>
<font></font>
## System Overview<font></font>
<font></font>
MCP-SSH is a Model Context Protocol server that provides SSH connection man=
agement capabilities to Claude Desktop.<font></font>
<font></font>
## Core Components<font></font>
<font></font>
### 1. SSHService<font></font>
<font></font>
Main class managing SSH connections.<font></font>
<font></font>
**Responsibilities:**<font></font>
- Connection lifecycle management<font></font>
- Credential storage and retrieval<font></font>
- Command execution<font></font>
- File transfer operations<font></font>
- Health monitoring<font></font>
<font></font>
**Key Methods:**<font></font>
- `connect()`: Establish new SSH connection<font></font>
- `executeCommand()`: Run command on remote server<font></font>
- `fileTransfer()`: Transfer files bidirectionally<font></font>
- `listConnections()`: Get all saved connections<font></font>
<font></font>
### 2. CircuitBreaker<font></font>
<font></font>
Prevents cascading failures and resource exhaustion.<font></font>
<font></font>
**States:**<font></font>
- Closed: Normal operation<font></font>
- Open: Failing fast without attempts<font></font>
- Half-Open: Testing if service recovered<font></font>
<font></font>
**Parameters:**<font></font>
- Failure threshold: 5 failures<font></font>
- Timeout: 60 seconds<font></font>
- Success threshold: 2 successes to close<font></font>
<font></font>
### 3. ExponentialBackoff<font></font>
<font></font>
Retry logic with increasing delays.<font></font>
<font></font>
**Parameters:**<font></font>
- Initial delay: 1000ms<font></font>
- Max delay: 300000ms (5 minutes)<font></font>
- Multiplier: 2x<font></font>
- Jitter: =C2=B120%<font></font>
<font></font>
### 4. Database Layer (LokiJS)<font></font>
<font></font>
Embedded NoSQL database for persistence.<font></font>
<font></font>
**Collections:**<font></font>
- `connections`: Connection metadata<font></font>
- `credentials`: Encrypted credentials (passwords)<font></font>
<font></font>
**Schema:**<font></font>
```typescript<font></font>
interface ConnectionDocument {<font></font>
  id: string;<font></font>
  name: string;<font></font>
  config: {<font></font>
    host: string;<font></font>
    port: number;<font></font>
    username: string;<font></font>
  };<font></font>
  lastUsed: Date;<font></font>
  tags: string[];<font></font>
  currentDirectory: string;<font></font>
}<font></font>
</code></pre>
<h2 class=3D"font-semibold" node=3D"[object Object]">Data Flow</h2>
<h3 class=3D"font-semibold" node=3D"[object Object]">Connection Establishme=
nt</h3>
<pre class=3D"bg-bg-200 p-3 rounded overflow-x-auto mb-2" node=3D"[object O=
bject]"><code class=3D"text-text-500" node=3D"[object Object]">User Request=
<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Validate Config<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Generate Connection ID (MD5 hash)<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Setup Credentials (Keychain/Database)<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Circuit Breaker Check<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Create SSH Client (ssh2 library)<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Setup Reconnect Logic<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Save to Database<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Return Connection Object<font></font>
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"font-semibold" node=3D"[object Object]">Command Execution</h3>
<pre class=3D"bg-bg-200 p-3 rounded overflow-x-auto mb-2" node=3D"[object O=
bject]"><code class=3D"text-text-500" node=3D"[object Object]">User Request=
 (connectionId + command)<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Load Connection from Database<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Circuit Breaker Check<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Execute via SSH Client<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Capture Output (stdout + stderr)<font></font>
    =E2=86=93<font></font>
Return Result<font></font>
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"font-semibold" node=3D"[object Object]">Error Handling Flow</h=
3>
