## Features:
### Secrets Manager:
- Algorithm: AES-256-GCM (strongest symmetric encryption)
- Key derivation: PBKDF2-SHA256, 100K iterations
- Random IV: 16 bytes per encryption
- Salt: 32 bytes per secret
- Authentication tags for integrity verification
- Zero-knowledge: master key never stored

### Security Features:
- File-based encrypted storage (0600 permissions)
- Master key from environment (MCP_MASTER_KEY)
- Auto-generates temporary key if not set
- Master key hashing for verification
- Test encryption/decryption functionality

### Capabilities:
- encrypt(): AES-256-GCM encryption with auth tag
- decrypt(): Authenticated decryption
- saveSecret(): Persist encrypted secret to file
- loadSecret(): Load and decrypt secret from file
- deleteSecret(): Securely delete secret file
- listSecrets(): List all stored secret IDs
- generateMasterKey(): Generate secure random key

### Use Cases:
- SSH passwords
- Private keys
- API tokens
- Database credentials
- Any sensitive configuration

## Configuration (.env.example):
- MCP_MASTER_KEY (required, never stored in code)
- SECRETS_ENABLED (default: true)
- SECRETS_DIR (default: ~/.mcp-ssh/secrets)
- SECRETS_PBKDF2_ITERATIONS (default: 100000)

## Dependencies:
- None! Uses built-in Node.js crypto

